        "subject": "LU-20791 efalnd: Track deactivated connections on a list",
        "message": "LU-20791 efalnd: Track deactivated connections on a list\n\nA deactivated connection was re-added to the hash table under key 0 so\nthe connection daemon could find it and clean it on the next daemon\ninvocation. On connection lookup, we search based on the remote NID\nwhich wasn't changed when the connection was re-inserted to the hash\ntable in deactivating state. A peer whose key falls in the same bucket\nstill matched it, so the caller got the dead connection. A send then\nleft its message pending on it until the daemon cancelled it, without\nstarting a new connection.\n\nThe impact is limited since the daemon removes the connection from the\nhash table at its next scan and then cancels its pending messages,\ncompleting them back to LNet with an error instead of leaving them\nstuck.\n\nRemove a deactivated connection from the hash table for good and queue\nit on a per-NI deactivate list protected by the connection hash lock.\nThe daemon's scan splices that list onto its cleanup list. The list\nreuses the connection's cleanup node, so a connection the scan already\ncollected as a candidate is moved off the candidate list and reaches\ncleanup in the same scan with its own teardown reason. With the key no\nlonger changing, the connection does not need to store it.\n\nFixes: 1720e4a88568 (\"LU-19693 efalnd: Use separate hash key in conn instead of remote NID\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\nChange-Id: I051097b746292950c80c5441aca79efe7538e3e0\n"
      },
